+   /* begonia: PANVK_HALVES: consecutive batches begin their polygon lists in the tiler heap's two halves in turn (every
+    * batch began at the heap's start, so a batch's tiler could not run while the batch before it was still drawn from
+    * its lists). The kernel's service reads the heap's base of a pixel job and of the chain behind it and runs them at
+    * once where they differ. Done once a batch: its template still has the whole heap. */
+   {
